# NestJS Server Package

## Structure

Keep chat/video symmetry:

- `*.module.ts` with `forRoot({ callbacks, customService })`
- `*.gateway.ts` for Socket.IO (`/call`, `/chat`)
- `*.service.ts` invoking callbacks
- `*.controller.ts` for thin REST mirrors
- `dtos/` + `interfaces/` for extension points
- Export public APIs from `src/index.ts`

## Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — validate payloads, ack clients, include server IDs
const saved = await this.chatService.saveMessage(...);
client.to(room).emit('newMessage', { ...saved, clientMessageId });
client.emit('messageAck', { ...saved, clientMessageId });
return { ok: true, message: saved };

// ❌ BAD — broadcast without messageId / ignore join failures
client.to(room).emit('newMessage', { message: data.message });
```

- Use Nest `Logger`, not ad-hoc `console.log` for gateway errors
- Optional `canConnect` callback gates handshakes; do not claim built-in auth
- Hang-up uses `CallStatus.ENDED`; decline uses `REJECTED`
- Specs live beside sources as `*.spec.ts` and are excluded from `tsc` emit
